      "summaryMarkdown": "The behaviour holds for RAYX-1..3, and the only defects are comment wording. Each key and value matches RayX.CLI docs/app-project.md: `version`, `[asset_package] id/kind/namespace`, `[assets] roots`, `[package.metadata.rayx.assets] manifest`, `android_java_dirs`, and the `android-platform`/`android-build-tools`/`android-ndk` keys of `[workspace.metadata.rayx]`. `android-system-image` and every other key are absent, and the tests reject extras through exact table lengths and key lists. The `assets` root holds `fonts/ibm-plex-sans/IBMPlexSans-Regular.ttf` and `fonts/lilex/Lilex-Regular.ttf`, the exact paths `load_bundled_fonts` (crates/gpui/src/svg_renderer.rs:312) loads through `AssetSource`. Every assertion can fail: they compare exact strings to `android::{COMPILE_SDK, BUILD_TOOLS_VERSION, NDK_VERSION, JAVA_SOURCES}` and to the parsed `ANDROID_PACKAGES` line, and the reads are unwrapped. Checks rerun: rayx_declarations 3/3 passed. The two package lists contain `rayx.assets.toml` and `java/dev/gpux/mobile/GpuxNativeActivity.java`. `cargo metadata --no-deps --offline` succeeded. No gpux source reads `metadata.rayx`, no manifest depends on rayx (the existing `rayx_diagnostics` features are only names), and nothing under vendor/ changed. `cargo package --workspace` (packaging rule for manifest changes) is left to the epic-end gate.",
